---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import LastVerified from '../../components/LastVerified.astro';
import SourceList from '../../components/SourceList.astro';
import AdsterraNativeBanner from '../../components/AdsterraNativeBanner.astro';
import { reportedRoster } from '../../data/characters';
import { sourceUrls, update110, update111 } from '../../data/sources';

const title = 'DragonSword Awakening Characters — Launch Roster & Ryza';
const description = 'Find the 19 launch Heroes, check how to unlock Ryza in Adventure Quest 53, find Othello’s Hero Quest, and check the announced release window for Jerome.';
const canonical = 'https://dragonswordguide.com/characters/';
const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: title, description,
  mainEntityOfPage: canonical, datePublished: '2026-08-08', dateModified: '2026-11-23',
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'DragonSword Guide' },
};
const sources = [
  { label: 'Steam store description', href: sourceUrls.steam, note: 'Launch Hero count and the story roles of Lute, Johnny and Castella.' },
  { label: 'Update 1.1.0', href: update110.href, note: 'Ryza’s quest reward and Shock effect, Othello’s Hero Log entry, and named Hero skill changes.' },
  { label: 'Update 1.1.1', href: update111.href, note: 'Fix for leveling Ryza on first login after clearing her quest.' },
  { label: 'Jerome’s official trailer announcement', href: 'https://steamcommunity.com/games/4570720/announcements/detail/562547437198114874', note: 'Free update planned for December 2026.' },
  { label: 'Developer roadmap and Q&A', href: sourceUrls.roadmap, note: 'Post-launch plans for Veronica and Logan.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} ogType="article" schema={[article]}>
  <div class="shell page-wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'DragonSword Guide', href: '/' }, { label: 'Characters' }]} />
    <article>
      <header class="article-header">
        <h1>DragonSword Awakening Characters</h1>
        <LastVerified label="Official sources checked" date="November 23, 2026" />
      </header>
      <section class="answer" aria-labelledby="ryza">
        <h2 id="ryza">How do I unlock Ryza?</h2>
        <p>Complete Adventure Quest #53, “Reunion,” to recruit Ryza. If you finished the quest before Update 1.1.0, the game grants her immediately. You can then open the Hero Codex for her skill details and introduction video.</p>
        <p>Ryza was added in Update 1.1.0 on October 15. Her spear attacks can inflict Shock. If you received her but could not level her up in the Hero menu on first login, Update 1.1.1 fixed that specific issue.</p>
        <figure>
          <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5nH_UPVyLCU">
            <img src="https://i.ytimg.com/vi/5nH_UPVyLCU/maxresdefault.jpg" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" alt="Ryza on the cover of the official DragonSword teaser" />
            <span>Watch Ryza’s teaser on YouTube</span>
          </a>
          <figcaption>Hound13’s character reveal for Ryza, the spear-wielding Hero awarded for “Reunion.”</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>The 19 launch Heroes</h2>
        <p>Look up a launch character by name below. In the opening story, Lute travels to Orbis and meets Johnny, a mercenary, and Castella, an Elf. Ryza joined after launch.</p>
        <ul class="names">{[...reportedRoster].sort().map(name => <li>{name}</li>)}</ul>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Where is Othello’s Hero Quest?</h2>
        <p>After completing Chapter 5, open <strong>Quests → Hero Log</strong> and select <em>What the Wind Asks</em>. This unlocks Othello’s story quest. The patch notes give no recruitment condition for Othello here.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>When are the next Heroes coming?</h2>
        <p>Hound13 announced Jerome for a free December 2026 update. The announcement gives a month only. Veronica and Logan also appear in the developer roadmap, with exact release dates and release order unknown. Check the <a href="/roadmap/">update timeline</a> for release announcements.</p>
        <figure>
          <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VLFUtQv25W4">
            <img src="https://i.ytimg.com/vi/VLFUtQv25W4/maxresdefault.jpg" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" alt="Jerome on the cover of the official DragonSword Hero Spotlight" />
            <span>Watch Jerome’s trailer on YouTube</span>
          </a>
          <figcaption>Hound13 introduces Jerome, the greatsword-wielding captain of the Lentus Rebellion’s strike team.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>
      <AdsterraNativeBanner />
      <SourceList sources={sources} intro="The roster uses the launch count from Steam and the Hero names in the official update notes. The quest conditions come from the developer’s release notes." />
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-wrap { padding: 1.25rem 0 2rem; }
  .article-header { max-width: 820px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  h1, h2 { line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -.04em; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 5rem); margin: 0 0 .7rem; }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 2rem); margin: 2rem 0 .7rem; }
  section { max-width: 760px; }
  section p { color: var(--muted-strong); }
  .answer { padding: 1rem 1.15rem; border: 1px solid hsl(199 86% 58% / .35); border-radius: 12px; background: var(--accent-soft); }
  .answer h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  .answer p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  figure { margin: 1.25rem 0 0; }
  figure img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 8px; }
  figure a { display: block; }
  figure a span { display: inline-block; margin-top: .45rem; text-decoration: underline; }
  figcaption { margin-top: .25rem; color: var(--muted-strong); font-size: .9rem; }
  .names { columns: 3; column-gap: 2rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .names li { padding: .15rem 0; break-inside: avoid; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .names { columns: 2; } }
</style>
